Abstract
In order to alleviate the problem of urban traffic congestion, the development of metro rail
transport has become the focus of underground space development in large and medium-sized
cities in China. Shield method has become a widely used and efficient construction method in
metro construction because it is suitable for soft water-bearing strata and complex construction
conditions. At the same time, however, the shield construction process is faced with many
problems such as complex geological environment, cumbersome construction process, etc., and
due to the long time in the hidden space operation, there are many safety hazards, resulting in the
shield method of construction safety accidents, which not only makes the benefits of the
construction project is damaged, but also to the safety of the personnel has brought a serious
threat. Qingdao Metro Line X shield interval in the construction process need to effectively deal
with multiple complex geological environments, such as granite, isolated rocks and strong
weathering strata, and the construction of the area where the water table is high, it is very easy to
cause soil liquefaction, gushing sand, gushing water, etc., which not only affects the normal
construction of the project, and may even cause casualties and property losses, so it is necessary
to evaluate the risk of the shield construction process, in order to provide reasonable and
scientific information for the follow-up of the project safety risk control. Therefore, it is
necessary to evaluate the risk of shield construction process in order to provide a reasonable and
scientific basis for the subsequent control of project safety risks. In view of this, this paper
explores the safety risk evaluation system suitable for the shield construction of Qingdao Metro
Line X from the perspective of the construction unit, aiming to strengthen the safety risk
management of the shield construction of the construction unit, and improve the ability of risk
prevention.
Firstly, based on the accident causation theory, accident statistical method and literature
research, the safety risk evaluation index system for shield construction of Qingdao Metro Line
X was constructed, and then the word cloud analysis was carried out by using the SPSSAU
software to screen out the high-frequency risk factors, and the initial risk list was established
accordingly. Then through the Delphi method combined with experts' professional knowledge
and rich experience, five primary indicators and 28 secondary indicators were finally determined,
including the risk of preparing for shield start, the risk of shield receiving and shaft construction,
the risk of normal shield digging, the risk of shield arrival and exit, and the risk of crossing
special sections.
Secondly, a risk evaluation model was constructed based on the BN network method, AHP


III
fuzzy comprehensive evaluation method and risk matrix. Using GeNIe 4.0 software, the
probability P that the overall risk of the project may occur was determined to be 56%.
Meanwhile, using the AHP-fuzzy comprehensive evaluation method, the overall risk loss value
of the project C was determined to be 51.44. Combined with the risk matrix of the improved
ALARP, the overall safety risk of the shield construction of Qingdao Metro Line X was
calculated to be rated as Class III, which is located in the lower limit area of ALARP, indicating
that the risk is within the acceptable interval.
Finally, the key risk factors for the total evaluation of the safety risk of shield construction
of Line X are put forward as practical risk management measures, aiming at the effective
prevention and control of risk occurrence. This paper evaluates the safety risk of shield
construction of Qingdao Metro Line X, aiming to provide a reasonable and scientific basis for
risk avoidance and subsequent risk management in the actual construction process, and at the
same time, provide a reference for the subsequent construction of other metro lines in Qingdao.
This paper has 36 figures, 26 tables, and 86 references.
Keywords: Qingdao metro; Shield construction; Safety risk; Bayesian network approach (BN);
AHP-fuzzy comprehensive evaluation


